          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Several law practices located in and around Brisbane’s Western Suburbs (Indooroopilly, the Centenary suburbs, and Kenmore) handle wills, estate litigation, and Family Provision Applications (FPAs) under the *Succession Act 1981* (Qld):\n\n---\n\n### 1. Firms Located Directly in the Western Suburbs / Centenary Area\n\n* **CG Legal Group (Indooroopilly)**\n  * **Focus:** Wills, estate administration, and estate disputes.\n  * **Litigation Services:** Specifically handles contested wills, Family Provision Applications (claims for inadequate maintenance/support), executor and beneficiary disputes, and testamentary capacity challenges. \n\n* **Kenmore Lawyers (Kenmore)**\n  * **Location:** Directly adjacent to Indooroopilly and the Centenary corridor.\n  * **Focus:** Full-service local practice with an established civil litigation and estates team (including senior practitioners with extensive Supreme and District Court litigation experience).\n  * **Litigation Services:** Family maintenance applications, disputing will validity (undue influence, lack of capacity), trust disputes, and attorney/EPOA disputes.\n\n* **Hawthorn Cuppaidge & Badgery Lawyers (Kenmore & Brisbane CBD)**\n  * **Location:** Branch office servicing Kenmore, Indooroopilly, and the western riverside suburbs.\n  * **Focus:** One of Queensland’s oldest established firms with a dedicated estate law practice.\n  * **Litigation Services:** Estate litigation, defending estates against claims, advising aggrieved family members on inheritance claims, and superannuation death-benefit disputes.\n\n* **Jindalee Lawyers / Steadfast Solicitors (Jindalee / Mount Ommaney)**\n  * **Location:** Based within the Centenary suburbs.\n  * **Focus:** General estate planning, administration, and probate disputes.\n  * **Litigation Services:** Advises local executors and excluded beneficiaries on early-stage estate disputes, mediations, and negotiating settlements prior to formal court litigation.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major Western Corridor & Inner-West Specialist Firms (Toowong / Milton)\nBecause larger estate litigation cases in Queensland proceed through the **Supreme Court of Queensland**, many specialized estate litigation firms serving Indooroopilly and Centenary residents base their offices slightly closer to the city hub along the western transport corridor:\n\n* **Australian Law Group (ALG) (Toowong)**\n  * **Location:** Coronation Drive / Sherwood Road hub (approx. 5 minutes from Indooroopilly).\n  * **Litigation Services:** Large litigation and estate practice handling contentious probate, FPA claims, and Supreme Court trials.\n* **Lockett McCullough Lawyers (Toowong & Surrounds)**\n  * **Services:** Regularly represents Western Suburbs clients in estate litigation, will challenges, and FPA mediation.\n\n---\n\n### What to Keep in Mind When Contacting a Western Suburbs Firm\n\n1. **Queensland Time Limits (Strict):**\n   * Under Queensland law (*Succession Act 1981*), an executor must receive **written notice of an intention to bring a Family Provision Application within 6 months** of the date of death.\n   * The formal originating application must be **filed in court within 9 months** of the date of death. \n2. **Fee Structures:**\n   * Many estate litigation firms take strong FPA or contested will matters on a **\"No Win, No Fee\"** or **deferred payment** basis (where legal fees are paid out of the final settlement or court-awarded estate proceeds). Ask upfront during your initial consultation what billing models they offer.\n3. **Executor Defense vs. Claimant Representation:**\n   * If you are an **executor** needing to defend the will against a family provision claim, ensure the firm has experience defending estates and negotiating resolutions via private mediation.",
